[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/banner.jpg[/img]

Cut-specific cooking for [b]Build 42[/b]. Every cut of meat has a best way to cook it and a best doneness, the dish is named after how you made it, and a meal cooked right lifts your mood. A Cooking window lays out every dish, pot, stove and drying rack within reach, and drying racks and a food dehydrator turn fresh fruit and vegetables into food that keeps for months. Works with vanilla food on its own, and with every Dazed Butchery cut and grade.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Yes, dedicated servers included[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Works with[/b][/td][td]Dazed Butchery, Dazed Climate, Dazed Power, Dazed Plumbing (all optional)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedCooking[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-cut.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/doneness.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/cuts.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Raw cuts say what they want in the tooltip, e.g. “Best: Grilled / Pan-seared, Medium rare – Medium”.
[*]Cook it in a stove or oven, on a barbecue, campfire or fireplace, or in a smoker. The method comes from where it cooked.
[*]Once it counts as cooked, the tooltip shows doneness live: Rare, Medium rare, Medium, Well done, Burnt.
[*]Take it out at the right moment. The dish is named for it: “Grilled Ribeye Steak (Choice, Medium rare)”.
[*]Eight kinds of cut, each with its own best method and doneness: steak, roast, slow, ribs, chop, pork roast, poultry and offal.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-mood.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/mood.png[/img]
[list]
[*]A cut cooked the right way to the right doneness lifts your mood and eases boredom and stress.
[*]Dazed Butchery's grade multiplies it: a Prime cut done right is the best meal you can have.
[*]A microwaved or burnt cut leaves you a little unhappy.
[*]With [b]Dazed Climate[/b], hot food eaten somewhere colder than 12 °C warms you for up to an hour, and a hot drink for up to half an hour.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-portion.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/portion.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Right-click a raw primal with a knife to cut it into portions: a Beef Rib becomes three Ribeye Steaks, a Pork Loin four Loin Chops, a Venison Backstrap four Medallions.
[*]Portions keep the primal's food, age and grade.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-window.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/window.png[/img]
Right-click a pot, pan, bowl or bread, a stove, oven, grill or fire, or a drying rack, and pick [b]Open Cooking Window[/b]. You can also bind a key in the Mods options.
[list]
[*][b]Cook[/b]: pick any of the game's dishes and a pot in reach, see every ingredient nearby with Butchery grades, [b]Add to pot[/b] with hunger and calories shown, then [b]Put on Stove[/b].
[*][b]On the Heat[/b]: everything cooking within 12 tiles, with doneness bars for cuts, cooking bars for pots, [b]Take Off[/b] and an optional burn warning.
[*][b]Recipes[/b]: save a pot as a named recipe, see what you have and what is missing, then [b]Cook Again[/b]. The book follows you between saves.
[*][b]Drying[/b]: every rack and dehydrator nearby, time left, what is ready, and Load and Collect buttons.
[*][b]Quick add[/b]: right-click a pot, [b]Add Ingredient[/b], pick the dish and use the + buttons.
[/list]
Every change goes through the game's own actions, so the window is multiplayer safe.

The in-game [b]Dazed Mod Suite Guide[/b] from Dazed Core has a Cooking tab.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-dry.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/dry.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Build a [b]Wooden Drying Rack[/b] (Carpentry 2) or a simple [b]Ground Drying Rack[/b] (no skill), place it like furniture and put fresh food in its 20 slots. It dries on its own.
[*]22 dried foods. Greens and mushrooms take 1 day, most fruit and vegetables 2, juicy fruit 3.
[*]Dried food weighs a quarter as much, keeps its calories and lasts for months. Use it in stews, soups, salads, cakes and pies. 1 Cooking XP each.
[*]The [b]Food Dehydrator[/b] (found in kitchens) dries three times as fast and ignores the weather. It needs the grid or a generator; with [b]Dazed Power[/b] it is a 500 W load. Its hum doesn't draw zombies.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/dry-more.png[/img]
[list]
[*]With [b]Dazed Climate[/b], outdoor racks pause in rain, snow and frost, slow in cold or damp, and dry faster in warm sun. A hardcore option (off by default) lets rain spoil rack food.
[*][b]Trail Mix[/b]: 3 dried fruit and a handful of nuts or seeds. [b]Fruit Leather[/b]: mash 3 ripe fruit in a bowl and dry it on a rack.
[*][b]Jerky[/b] (with Dazed Butchery): Make Jerky gives Salted Meat Strips to dry on a rack, in the dehydrator or in Dazed Plumbing's smoker.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-sandbox.png[/img]
11 options: Good Food Mood Bonus (0 turns it off), Named Dishes, Cooking Tips in Tooltips, Hot Food Warms You, Drying Speed, Dried Food Shelf Life, Weather Affects Drying Racks, Rain Spoils Rack Food, Dehydrator Watts, Dehydrator Loot Rarity and Jerky Needs Drying. The burn warning and the window's key are player options on the Dazed page of the Mods options.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-compat.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Build 42 only.
[*]Vanilla meat works without Dazed Butchery; Butchery adds its cuts, grades, portioning and jerky to dry.
[*]Hot food warmth and rack weather need [b]Dazed Climate[/b]. Without it racks dry at a fixed speed.
[*]Builds on the game's own cooking, evolved recipes and timed actions. The server runs all drying.
[*]The window can't take an ingredient back out of a pot, because the game can't either.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Cooking/images/h-help.png[/img]
Post in the Discussions tab. Include your game version, the Dazed mods you run, and your console.txt if there is an error.

